{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You have skirted this mountain long enough.</b> He restrained them from provoking the children of Esau, because he honored his father, and the Holy One, blessed be He, does not withhold the reward of any creature — and so that he may not have an opening for complaint in the World to Come, for he has already taken his reward in this world." "<b>Turn yourselves northward.</b> They said in the Midrash Rabbah: if the hour of Esau comes, hide yourselves away from before him, as it is said, ״Turn yourselves northward (פנו לכם צפונה)״. Another matter: ״Turn yourselves northward״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: I have one altar, and it is destined to abandon it. Another matter: ״Turn yourselves northward״ — I had one צפון (hidden treasure) among you, namely the Holy Temple, in which I was hidden away with you, and it is destined to destroy it, as it is said (Ezekiel 7:22): ״והסבותי פני מהם וחללו את צפוני״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:48.834773167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}